sentences.l:
“At dawn indeed, even more, the exceeding-strong son of Cronus
you will see, if you wish, ox-eyed lady Hera,
destroying of the Argive spearmen a great host;

And let heralds up and down the town, dear to Zeus, announce
that boys in first youth and grey-templed old men
lay themselves down about the town on the god-built towers;

but among the foremost, I think,
he will lie stabbed, and around him many companions,
when the sun rises, on the morrow;
